> diff abs(x)
d/dx abs(x) = sign(x)
  holds for x != 0
    at x = 0 abs(x) has a corner (slope -1 from the left, 1 from the right)
    (points looked for in [-10, 10])
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 1e-15)
> diff sqrt(x)
d/dx sqrt(x) = 0.5/sqrt(x)
  holds for x > 0
    at x = 0 (an end of the domain) sqrt(x) has an infinite one-sided slope
    (points looked for in [-10, 10])
  check: matches central differences at 100 points (max relative difference 6e-14)
> diff log(x)
d/dx log(x) = 1/x
  holds for x > 0
  check: matches central differences at 100 points (max relative difference 2e-13)
> diff x*abs(x) x 2
d/dx x*abs(x) = abs(x) + x*sign(x)
d²/dx² x*abs(x) = 2sign(x)
  holds for x != 0
    at x = 0 d/dx x*abs(x) has a corner (slope -2 from the left, 2 from the right)
    (points looked for in [-10, 10])
  check: each order matches central differences at 402 points (max relative difference 2e-15)
> diff sin(x) x 3
d/dx sin(x) = cos(x)
d²/dx² sin(x) = -sin(x)
d³/dx³ sin(x) = -cos(x)
  holds for every real x
  check: each order matches central differences at 603 points (max relative difference 3e-15)
> diff x^3 2
d/dx x^3 = 3x^2
d²/dx² x^3 = 6x
  holds for every real x
  check: each order matches central differences at 402 points (max relative difference 2e-15)
> diff floor(x) + x^2
d/dx floor(x) + x^2 = 2x
  holds for x not an integer
    where x is an integer it jumps (no derivative there)
    (points looked for in [-10, 10])
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 2e-15)
> diff max(x, x^2)
d/dx max(x, x^2) = x >= x^2 ? 1 : 2x
  holds for x != 0 and x != 1
    at x = 0 max(x, x^2) has a corner (slope 0 from the left, 1 from the right)
    at x = 1 max(x, x^2) has a corner (slope 1 from the left, 2 from the right)
    (points looked for in [-10, 10])
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 2e-15)
> diff x^(1/3)
d/dx x^0.3333333333 = x^(-0.6666666667)/3
  holds for x > 0
    at x = 0 (an end of the domain) x^0.3333333333 has an infinite one-sided slope
    (points looked for in [-10, 10])
  check: matches central differences at 100 points (max relative difference 1e-13)
> myabs(x: real) = x > 0 ? x : -x
> diff myabs
d/dx myabs = x > 0 ? 1 : -1
  holds for x != 0
    at x = 0 myabs has a corner (slope -1 from the left, 1 from the right)
    (points looked for in [-10, 10])
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 1e-15)
> g(x) = x^3 - x
> g''
d/dx g = 3x^2 - 1
d²/dx² g = 6x
  holds for every real x
  check: each order matches central differences at 402 points (max relative difference 2e-15)
> g'(2)
g'(2) = 11
  from g' = 3x^2 - 1
> myabs'(0)
myabs'(0) does not exist: at x = 0 myabs has a corner (slope -1 from the left, 1 from the right)
> diff exp(2x) n
d^n/dx^n exp(2x) = exp(2x)*2^n
  holds for every real x and n >= 0; check: equals the derivatives of orders 1..6 at 120 points
> diff sin(3x) n
d^n/dx^n sin(3x) = 3^n*sin(3x + n*pi/2)
  holds for every real x and n >= 0; check: equals the derivatives of orders 1..6 at 120 points
> diff log(2x + 1) n
d^n/dx^n log(2x + 1) = (-1)^(n - 1) (n - 1)! 2^n / (2x + 1)^n  for n >= 1
  holds for x > -1/2; check: equals the derivatives of orders 1..6 at 120 points
> diff 1/(2x + 1) n
d^n/dx^n 1/(2x + 1) = -1(-1 - 1)...(-1 - n + 1) 2^n (2x + 1)^(-1 - n)
  holds where 2x + 1 != 0; check: equals the derivatives of orders 1..6 at 120 points
> diff x^5 n
  note: x^5 is a polynomial of degree 5: its derivatives of order > 5 are 0
d^n/dx^n x^5 = 5(5 - 1)...(5 - n + 1) x^(5 - n)
  holds for every real x and 0 <= n <= 5 (0 for n > 5); check: equals the derivatives of orders 1..6 at 120 points
> diff x^2*y x
∂/∂x x^2*y = 2x*y
  holds wherever the formula is defined
  check: matches central differences at 100 points (max relative difference 3e-13)
> diff x^2*y^3 x y
∂²/∂y∂x x^2*y^3 = 6x*y^2
  holds wherever the formula is defined
  check: each order matches central differences at 200 points (max relative difference 3e-13)
> diff x^2*y
  note: x^2*y has 2 variables (x, y): all first partial derivatives, the gradient (say `diff F x` for one)
∇ x^2*y = (2x*y, x^2)
  ∂/∂x x^2*y = 2x*y
  ∂/∂y x^2*y = x^2
  holds wherever the formulas are defined
  check: every entry matches central differences at 200 points (max relative difference 4e-13)
> partial x*y^2 y
∂/∂y x*y^2 = 2x*y
  holds wherever the formula is defined
  check: matches central differences at 100 points (max relative difference 3e-13)
> diff sqrt(x^2 + y^2) x
∂/∂x sqrt(x^2 + y^2) = x/sqrt(x^2 + y^2)
  holds for x^2 + y^2 >= 0
    may fail where x^2 + y^2 = 0 (an infinite slope)
  check: matches central differences at 100 points (max relative difference 5e-12)
> f(x, y) = x^2*y + y^3
> fx
∂/∂x f = 2x*y
  holds wherever the formula is defined
  check: matches central differences at 100 points (max relative difference 4e-13)
> fxy
∂²/∂y∂x f = 2x
  holds wherever the formula is defined
  check: each order matches central differences at 200 points (max relative difference 4e-13)
> diff x y
  note: y is not a variable of x: read as a product (for a derivative wrt y write `diff F wrt y`)
  note: x*y has 2 variables (x, y): all first partial derivatives, the gradient (say `diff F x` for one)
∇ x*y = (y, x)
  ∂/∂x x*y = y
  ∂/∂y x*y = x
  holds wherever the formulas are defined
  check: every entry matches central differences at 200 points (max relative difference 3e-13)
> grad x^2*y + sin(y)
∇ x^2*y + sin(y) = (2x*y, x^2 + cos(y))
  ∂/∂x x^2*y + sin(y) = 2x*y
  ∂/∂y x^2*y + sin(y) = x^2 + cos(y)
  holds wherever the formulas are defined
  check: every entry matches central differences at 200 points (max relative difference 5e-13)
> grad x^2 + y^2 at 1, 2
∇ x^2 + y^2 = (2x, 2y)
  ∂/∂x x^2 + y^2 = 2x
  ∂/∂y x^2 + y^2 = 2y
  holds wherever the formulas are defined
  check: every entry matches central differences at 200 points (max relative difference 4e-13)
  at (x = 1, y = 2): (2, 4), |∇| = 4.472135955
> hessian x^2 - y^2 at 0, 0
Hessian of x^2 - y^2 (row i, column j: ∂²/∂j∂i):
  [ 2   0  ]   ∂/∂x
  [ 0   -2 ]   ∂/∂y
  det = -4
  holds wherever the formulas are defined
  check: every entry matches central differences at 400 points (max relative difference 2e-13)
  symmetric (the mixed partials agree) at 100 of 100 sample pairs
  at (x = 0, y = 0):
  [ 2          0          ]
  [ 0          -2         ]
  det = -4
  the gradient is 0 and the Hessian is indefinite: a saddle point
> hessian x^2 + y^2 at (0, 0)
Hessian of x^2 + y^2 (row i, column j: ∂²/∂j∂i):
  [ 2   0 ]   ∂/∂x
  [ 0   2 ]   ∂/∂y
  det = 4
  holds wherever the formulas are defined
  check: every entry matches central differences at 400 points (max relative difference 2e-13)
  symmetric (the mixed partials agree) at 100 of 100 sample pairs
  at (x = 0, y = 0):
  [ 2          0          ]
  [ 0          2          ]
  det = 4
  the gradient is 0 and the Hessian is positive definite (leading minors > 0): a local minimum
> hessian x^3 - 3x*y^2 at 0, 0
Hessian of x^3 - 3x*y^2 (row i, column j: ∂²/∂j∂i):
  [ 6x    -6y ]   ∂/∂x
  [ -6y   -6x ]   ∂/∂y
  det = -36x^2 - 36y^2
  holds wherever the formulas are defined
  check: every entry matches central differences at 400 points (max relative difference 4e-13)
  symmetric (the mixed partials agree) at 100 of 100 sample pairs
  at (x = 0, y = 0):
  [ 0          0          ]
  [ 0          0          ]
  det = 0
  the gradient is 0 but the Hessian is singular: the second-derivative test is inconclusive
> laplacian x^2 - y^2
∇² x^2 - y^2 = 0
  ∂²/∂x² x^2 - y^2 = 2
  ∂²/∂y² x^2 - y^2 = -2
  holds wherever the formulas are defined
  check: every entry matches central differences at 400 points (max relative difference 4e-13)
  x^2 - y^2 is harmonic: its Laplacian is 0 at all 200 sample points (and symbolically 0)
