> wronskian sin(x), cos(x)
Wronskian matrix of sin(x), cos(x) (row k: the k-th derivatives wrt x)
  [ sin(x)   cos(x)  ]   the functions
  [ cos(x)   -sin(x) ]   d/dx
  W = det = -sin(x)^2 - cos(x)^2
  W = -1  (equal to the determinant at all 200 sample points of [-10, 10])
  check: every entry matches central differences at 402 points (max relative difference 3e-15)
  linearly independent: W(-1/20) = -1 != 0, so the functions are independent on every interval containing x = -1/20
> wronskian exp(x), exp(2x), exp(3x)
Wronskian matrix of exp(x), exp(2x), exp(3x) (row k: the k-th derivatives wrt x)
  [ exp(x)   exp(2x)    exp(3x)  ]   the functions
  [ exp(x)   2exp(2x)   3exp(3x) ]   d/dx
  [ exp(x)   4exp(2x)   9exp(3x) ]   d²/dx²
  W = det = 2exp(6x)
  check: every entry matches central differences at 1206 points (max relative difference 2e-13)
  linearly independent: W(-1/20) = 1.481636441 != 0, so the functions are independent on every interval containing x = -1/20
> wronskian 1, x, x^2
Wronskian matrix of 1, x, x^2 (row k: the k-th derivatives wrt x)
  [ 1   x   x^2 ]   the functions
  [ 0   1   2x  ]   d/dx
  [ 0   0   2   ]   d²/dx²
  W = det = 2
  check: every entry matches central differences at 1206 points (max relative difference 2e-15)
  linearly independent: W(-1/20) = 2 != 0, so the functions are independent on every interval containing x = -1/20
> wronskian x, 2x
Wronskian matrix of x, 2x (row k: the k-th derivatives wrt x)
  [ x   2x ]   the functions
  [ 1   2  ]   d/dx
  W = det = 0
  check: every entry matches central differences at 402 points (max relative difference 1e-15)
  W = 0 at all 200 sample points
  a linear relation holds at all 200 points: -2*(x) + (2x) = 0
  linearly dependent (the functions are analytic, so W = 0 everywhere implies dependence; the relation confirms it)
> wronskian x^2, x*abs(x)
Wronskian matrix of x^2, x*abs(x) (row k: the k-th derivatives wrt x)
  [ x^2   x*abs(x)           ]   the functions
  [ 2x    abs(x) + x*sign(x) ]   d/dx
  W = det = x^3*sign(x) - x^2*abs(x)
  W = 0  (equal to the determinant at all 200 sample points of [-10, 10])
  check: every entry matches central differences at 402 points (max relative difference 2e-15)
  W = 0 at all 200 sample points
  W = 0 does not prove dependence for functions that are not analytic (x^2 and x*abs(x) have W = 0 and are independent), and no linear relation fits their values: independent on [-10, 10]
> wronskian sin(x)^2, cos(x)^2, 1
Wronskian matrix of sin(x)^2, cos(x)^2, 1 (row k: the k-th derivatives wrt x)
  [ sin(x)^2                cos(x)^2                1 ]   the functions
  [ 2sin(x)*cos(x)          -(2sin(x)*cos(x))       0 ]   d/dx
  [ 2cos(x)^2 - 2sin(x)^2   2sin(x)^2 - 2cos(x)^2   0 ]   d²/dx²
  W = det = 0
  check: every entry matches central differences at 1206 points (max relative difference 3e-14)
  W = 0 at all 200 sample points
  a linear relation holds at all 200 points: -(sin(x)^2) - (cos(x)^2) + (1) = 0
  linearly dependent (the functions are analytic, so W = 0 everywhere implies dependence; the relation confirms it)
